==========================================
V3.1 VRON ARCHITECTURE
==========================================

Core Philosophy
---------------
The engine should not consist of many specialized modules (Responder, Reactor,
Planner, Weaver, etc.).

Instead, the engine only understands one primitive:

    VRon (Virtual Neuron)

A VRon is an ephemeral reasoning process.

It is born, performs a single cognitive task, leaves behind facts,
then disappears.

Behavior emerges from context rather than hardcoded modules.


==========================================
ENGINE
==========================================

Engine
│
├── Scheduler
├── Spawn Queue (rate limiter)
├── Memory Graph
├── Retriever
└── VRons (spawned dynamically)

The Scheduler is deterministic.

It only decides whether a new VRon should exist.

Examples:
- User sent a message
- Context exceeded threshold
- Sleep cycle
- Pending tests exist
- Background processing required


==========================================
VRON
==========================================

A VRon has NO permanent role.

It is not:
- a responder
- a summarizer
- a planner
- a dreamer

Instead,

its CURRENT CONTEXT determines its goal.

Examples:

User asks question
→ Goal = Respond

Conversation too large
→ Goal = Summarize

Need more information
→ Goal = Retrieve Memory

Need contradiction checking
→ Goal = Test Facts

Need logical reasoning
→ Goal = Execute Logic

Need relation weaving
→ Goal = Build Relations

[OPEN QUESTION — not yet resolved]
What actually performs goal-determination?
  (a) a cheap deterministic classifier (keyword / embedding routing), or
  (b) an LLM call ("given this context, what should I do")
If (b), this call counts against the spawn/energy budget below —
it is itself a VRon-equivalent cost, not a free step.


==========================================
VRON LIFECYCLE
==========================================

Spawn (queued — see Spawn Queue)

↓

Read Context

↓

Determine Goal

↓

Execute

↓

Spawn child VRons if needed

↓

Return Facts

↓

Destroy


VRons never persist.

Only the facts they generate persist.


==========================================
SPAWN QUEUE (RATE LIMITING)
==========================================

Depth is intentionally left UNBOUNDED. It does not need a hard cap because
of the natural terminator described below. What must be bounded instead is
CALL RATE, since every VRon (other than pure-embedding goals) is a real LLM
call against a real, limited quota.

Mechanism: token-bucket spawn queue.
- N spawns permitted per time window.
- Excess spawn requests wait for the next window.
- Applies globally across all VRon goal types.

Priority tiers within the queue:
- TIER 1 (highest): VRons descending from an active, user-triggered
  Respond-goal chain. The user is waiting; this chain should not be
  starved by background work.
- TIER 2: background/idle-triggered chains (Weaver passes, gap-detection,
  sleep-cycle consolidation, etc).

Cost weighting (energy, not just rate):
- Retrieve-goal VRons are cheap (embedding-only calls where possible).
- Test-goal, Respond-goal, and Logic-authoring VRons are full LLM calls
  and should draw proportionally more from the shared Mental Energy pool.
- Energy MUST be a single shared pool across the whole engine, not
  scoped per-VRon or per-chain — this is what makes a deep chain
  naturally self-limiting (a long chain costs proportionally more and
  will exhaust the pool and throttle on its own).


==========================================
NATURAL TERMINATION (why unbounded depth is safe)
==========================================

A Retrieve-goal VRon has exactly two terminal outcomes:
  1. Finds the needed fact → done.
  2. Finds nothing → returns UNKNOWN → done.

There is no third branch where a VRon spawns another Retrieve to "search
harder." UNKNOWN is itself one of the four fixed Test outcomes (see below)
and is a leaf, not a branch. This means a well-formed chain bottoms out in
a small, predictable number of hops on its own. The spawn queue above is a
backstop against BURST traffic (many small chains arriving close together),
not a defense against any single chain running away — that path is closed
by construction.


==========================================
VRON COMMUNICATION
==========================================

VRons may spawn other VRons.

Example

VRon
Goal:
Respond

↓

Needs more memory

↓

Spawn VRon

Goal:
Retrieve Memory

↓

Returns Facts

↓

Dies

↓

Parent continues.


Likewise

VRon

↓

Needs contradiction testing

↓

Spawn Test VRon

↓

Returns

PASS / FAIL / CONFLICT / UNKNOWN

↓

Dies


==========================================
VRON OUTPUT
==========================================

Every VRon produces facts.

The status of its reasoning is always one of

PASS
FAIL
CONFLICT
UNKNOWN (Insufficient Information)

Those outputs become graph mutations.


==========================================
TEST -> RESULT ARCHITECTURE
==========================================

Everything in cognition is treated as a Test.

Each Test is itself a VRon: a full, independently-scoped LLM call given
only the two nodes under comparison (plus minimal supporting context) as
its entire world. It returns one of the four fixed outcomes, then dies.
No persistence, no memory of itself — a disposable judgment instance.

Inputs

↓

Test

↓

PASS / FAIL / CONFLICT / UNKNOWN

↓

Graph Mutation

↓

New Fact


OUTCOME RULES (deterministic, based on stored node strength —
not an LLM judgment call):

PASS
  → Both nodes consistent. Strengthen both.

FAIL
  → A high-strength node invalidates a LOWER-strength node.
  → The weaker node fails. Clear winner, no ambiguity.

CONFLICT
  → A high-strength node is tested against ANOTHER high-strength node
    (weights within some delta of each other — exact delta TBD by tuning).
  → Neither side has grounds to auto-win. This is reserved for genuinely
    rare, high-stakes disagreements between two things that each already
    earned real confidence — NOT for routine mismatches. Maps to a
    Cortisol spike (see Mindstate Mapping below).
  → CONFLICT does not auto-resolve toward the heavier-weighted side.
    If it did, it would just be FAIL with extra steps, and the
    "irrational/unresolved tension" behavior would never surface.

UNKNOWN
  → Insufficient data to run the test at all.
  → Maps to UA (uncertainty) rising — NOT to MA (attention) falling.
    An unanswered question should read as active curiosity about a
    missing piece, not disinterest.
  → Becomes a Planned Test (see below).


PROVENANCE AND TRUST FLOOR (applies to FAIL / CONFLICT resolution):
  A node's high strength can originate from two different places:
    (a) directly user-stated
    (b) self-derived, reinforced through internal Test passes over time
  These are NOT equal footing at equal weight. A self-derived node has
  already passed through at least one fallible LLM inference step; a
  user-stated node is closer to ground truth about what the user
  actually said. Self-derived nodes should require a HIGHER strength
  threshold than user-stated nodes before they're allowed to resist
  contradiction from that user — otherwise the engine can end up
  confidently overriding a user's own stated preference with something
  it hallucinated and then reinforced into false confidence.

ARGUING DOWN A HIGH-STRENGTH FACT (user pushes back on a held belief):
  - Triggers a Test VRon: existing fact (Node A) vs. the user's new
    argument, freshly created as a node (Node B).
  - A winning argument DECREMENTS the held fact's weight rather than
    flipping it outright — reversal should take sustained, accumulated
    pushback, not one good line, matching the asymmetric-friction
    behavior used elsewhere in this system.
  - Tone of concession is decided by WHETHER THE WINNING ARGUMENT
    CONTAINED GENUINELY NEW INFORMATION:
      - New information present → graceful concession (legitimate
        epistemic update).
      - No new information, weight simply eroded by repetition →
        reluctant / "pissed" concession (worn down, not persuaded).
    This is a concrete, checkable branch, not a tonal coin flip.

CONTRADICTION IN SELF-GENERATED DIRECTIVES (e.g. "do X, not Y" later
conflicting with "do Y, not X"):
  - This does NOT require graph-cycle-detection machinery.
  - Directives must be reified as their own stored, testable nodes at
    the moment they're generated (not left implicit in response prose).
  - An ordinary pairwise Test between two directive-nodes, with
    CONFLICT as a legitimate outcome, catches direct adjacent
    contradictions on its own.
  - Known limitation: this only catches DIRECT pairwise contradictions.
    A longer indirect chain (A rules out B, B rules out C, C rules out
    D, D rules out A, with no two adjacent nodes directly opposing)
    would not necessarily surface via pairwise semantic-similarity
    testing, since non-adjacent nodes may not be embedding-close.
    Not solved in v3.1 — flagged for later if it turns out to matter.


==========================================
MINDSTATE MAPPING
==========================================

PASS      → reinforces weight of tested nodes (stubbornness / momentum)
FAIL      → weaker node's weight decreases
CONFLICT  → Cortisol spike (genuine, rare, earned tension)
UNKNOWN   → UA (uncertainty) rises, NOT MA falling

Boredom / decreasing interest (MA decay):
  Triggered by Test redundancy — repeatedly running the same or highly
  similar Tests against the same semantic region with predictable PASS
  results. If nothing novel is being tested, MA decays. This produces
  context-driven disinterest without needing it hardcoded into the
  personality prompt.


==========================================
PLANNED TESTS
==========================================

If a test returns UNKNOWN, it is not discarded.

It becomes a pending test.

Future conversations automatically attempt to complete it when new
information arrives. The result of one Test may also spawn a new,
deeper Test, creating chains of long-term goals that can span multiple
sessions.


==========================================
META CONTEXT (supersession, not overwrite)
==========================================

When a Result changes or replaces an earlier Result, the earlier one is
NOT deleted. It is marked as superseded-by the new Result, preserving a
traceable chain. This is what allows the engine to answer "why did this
fact change" — the answer is the chain itself, not a separate log.

Consistent with the general rule used throughout this system: rejected
or replaced data gets quarantined/marked, never silently deleted.


==========================================
MEMORY GRAPH
==========================================

Conversation

↓

Fact Nodes

↓

Relation Nodes

↓

Summary Nodes

↓

Model Nodes


The graph continuously evolves.

Everything is represented as nodes.

The node itself never stores "its type".

Its meaning emerges from its contents
and graph connectivity.


==========================================
WEAVER
==========================================

Originally a standalone module.

Now simply another goal a VRon can perform.

Input:
Fact Node

↓

Find semantically similar nodes

↓

Generate Proto Relations

↓

Responder validates

↓

Successful relations become permanent nodes.

Negative results (a relation the Responder identifies as false /
hallucinated) are NOT deleted either — flagged as a permanent negative
relation so the same false connection is not independently re-derived
later just because the two nodes remain embedding-close.


==========================================
SUMMARIZATION
==========================================

Summary generation is triggered
when conversation/history grows.

Instead of loading dozens of facts into context,

the engine creates Summary Nodes.

Summary Nodes become shortcuts through the graph.

Future retrieval can use summaries
instead of traversing every fact.


==========================================
MODEL NODES
==========================================

Repeated summaries naturally evolve.

Facts

↓

Relations

↓

Summaries

↓

Models

Models are abstractions of large regions
of the memory graph.

They are not hardcoded.

They emerge naturally.

REQUIRED SAFEGUARDS (carried over from earlier personality-layer design —
apply here too, do not treat as solved just because this section is new):
  - Weight/strength used for Model formation MUST decay over time or
    include recency weighting. Without decay, early-formed Models
    accumulate strength fastest purely by having existed longest,
    crowding out newer, possibly more accurate abstractions
    (rich-get-richer convergence).
  - A candidate Model should be checked for compatibility against the
    engine's immutable core identity before being allowed to become
    dominant/active — high internal reinforcement alone is not
    sufficient grounds for a Model to override core-identity behavior.


==========================================
DEPTH RETRIEVAL
==========================================

Retriever gains depth.

Level 1
→ Summary

Level 2
→ Relations

Level 3
→ Individual facts

Meaning:

The engine can request more detail
only when needed,
keeping token usage low.

[OPEN QUESTION — not yet resolved]
What triggers a request for deeper detail? Likely candidate: the
Respond-goal VRon receives the Level 1 summary first, and only spawns
a deeper-retrieval VRon if its own confidence/completeness is
insufficient at that level — but the concrete trigger for "insufficient"
still needs to be pinned to something checkable, not left as a vibe.


==========================================
SELF EVOLUTION
==========================================

Because everything is represented
as facts and tests,

the engine gradually evolves:

Facts

↓

Relations

↓

Summaries

↓

Models

↓

New Tests

↓

New Facts

The abstraction process never stops.


==========================================
V3 (LOGIC EXECUTION)
==========================================

Logic execution will be added.

VRons may write tiny JavaScript programs
for deterministic reasoning.

Examples

- counting
- addition
- boolean logic
- wikipedia retrieval
- custom skills

Generated functions are stored
as Logic Nodes.

Future prompts reuse them
without needing the LLM again.

NOTE (carried over, still applies):
  A cached Logic Node must be verified against known input/output pairs
  before being trusted for reuse — determinism guarantees the execution
  is trustworthy, not that the generated program is correct. Retrieval
  of a cached Logic Node for reuse should match on exact structure/
  variables involved, not just embedding similarity, since a
  semantically similar logical statement is not necessarily a logically
  equivalent one.


==========================================
DESIGN PRINCIPLES
==========================================

• Minimal number of engine primitives
• Context determines behavior
• Everything becomes facts
• Memory is graph-based
• Emergent behavior over handcrafted modules
• Short-lived VRons
• Persistent memory only exists in the graph
• Progressive abstraction:
  Facts → Relations → Summaries → Models
• Token efficiency through graph shortcuts
• One deterministic scheduler
• Many temporary reasoning cells
• Rejected/superseded data is quarantined, never silently deleted
• Depth is unbounded; RATE is bounded (spawn queue + shared energy pool)
• Nothing is trusted into dominance by reinforcement alone — coherence
  against the immutable core is a separate, required check

